From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 23:46:14 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/1] wifi: ath12k: no warning when the RX channel fallback is
 the expected one

On a WCN7860 station on 5 GHz (channel 36, VHT80), once station power
save has been applied in the boot (also after it is switched off again
at run time), the RX PHY metadata of most frames during a large transfer
carries an invalid channel number (233) with the right centre frequency
of the 80 MHz channel (5210 MHz). ath12k_dp_rx_h_ppdu() then finds no
band, warns "sband is NULL for status band 6 channel_num 233 center_freq
5210" and falls back to ar->rx_channel, which gives the right band and
frequency: the frame is delivered normally. The rate-limited warning
fires about 200 000 times per 300 MB received.

Keep the fallback. Warn only when the metadata's centre frequency is not
within 160 MHz (half the widest channel) of the RX channel or when there
is no RX channel; otherwise report it with dev_dbg_ratelimited(), which
dynamic debug can switch on (ath12k_dbg() is compiled out without
CONFIG_ATH12K_DEBUG, which this kernel does not set).
The warning prints the values from the metadata, not the fallback's.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp_rx.c | 27 ++++++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp_rx.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp_rx.c
index c7b371e824d6..97d2d88d4018 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp_rx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp_rx.c
@@ -1439,13 +1439,22 @@ void ath12k_dp_rx_h_ppdu(struct ath12k_pdev_dp *dp_pdev,
 	if (unlikely(rx_status->band == NUM_NL80211_BANDS ||
 		     !ath12k_pdev_dp_to_hw(dp_pdev)->wiphy->bands[rx_status->band])) {
 		struct ath12k *ar = ath12k_pdev_dp_to_ar(dp_pdev);
-
-		ath12k_warn(ar->ab, "sband is NULL for status band %d channel_num %d center_freq %d pdev_id %d\n",
-			    rx_status->band, channel_num, center_freq, ar->pdev_idx);
+		int st_band = rx_status->band;
+		u8 st_chan = channel_num;
+		bool expected = false;
 
 		spin_lock_bh(&ar->data_lock);
 		channel = ar->rx_channel;
 		if (channel) {
+			/*
+			 * Some firmware leaves the channel number of the PHY
+			 * metadata invalid while its centre frequency (the
+			 * centre of the whole operating channel) is right. If
+			 * that frequency lies within the widest channel around
+			 * the current RX channel, the fallback below is the
+			 * expected answer: no warning for every such frame.
+			 */
+			expected = abs((int)center_freq - (int)channel->center_freq) <= 160;
 			rx_status->band = channel->band;
 			channel_num =
 				ieee80211_frequency_to_channel(channel->center_freq);
@@ -1455,6 +1464,18 @@ void ath12k_dp_rx_h_ppdu(struct ath12k_pdev_dp *dp_pdev,
 			ath12k_err(ar->ab, "unable to determine channel, band for rx packet");
 		}
 		spin_unlock_bh(&ar->data_lock);
+
+		/*
+		 * dynamic debug (file dp_rx.c +p): ath12k_dbg() is compiled
+		 * out without CONFIG_ATH12K_DEBUG
+		 */
+		if (expected)
+			dev_dbg_ratelimited(ar->ab->dev,
+					    "rx: invalid channel_num %d, center_freq %d, using the rx channel\n",
+					    st_chan, center_freq);
+		else
+			ath12k_warn(ar->ab, "sband is NULL for status band %d channel_num %d center_freq %d pdev_id %d\n",
+				    st_band, st_chan, center_freq, ar->pdev_idx);
 		goto h_rate;
 	}
 
